What to Check Before Choosing Any Offshore Host
Not every provider that markets itself around privacy actually delivers the same level of protection once a real complaint lands.

Check whether the provider handles abuse reports directly or routes them through a third party.
Look closely at whether shared or WordPress hosting is actually available, or whether you are being pushed into a VPS you may not need.
Compare specs against price rather than trusting the marketing copy alone.
Confirm the actual data center location and jurisdiction, since this determines which local laws genuinely apply to your content.
Ask directly about support response times before you sign up, not after something breaks.
Read the acceptable use policy in full rather than skimming the marketing page.
